== H. The pullback mechanism (Inselmann arXiv:2402.03276 Lemma 2.16), no mixing used ==
   T^k m = 3^a m / 2^k + offset.  Given M = T^k m and a, m lies in an interval of length (offset+1) 2^k / 3^a.
   So the law of M has density at most about k max(offset) / range against uniform, hence
   P_m(T^k m in B) <= k 2^(eps k) 3^(-D k/2)-style bounds for any B of power-saving density X^(-D).
